// Sealed Ward - one cell, repeated, with the harmony moving above it.
//
// This is an ostinato piece, not a chord progression, because that is what the
// measurements said. Across ten Masuko-era SNES scores the bass repeats a 2- to
// 4-bar cell at 100% exactness for the whole track, the harmony is four or five
// pitch classes used subtractively, and everything moves in sixteenths. A riff
// that turns around onto a new chord every bar is rock writing; this idiom
// pedals, and the interest comes from what is laid over the pedal.
//
// So: the bass plays the same two bars from the first downbeat to the last,
// never once varying its pitches. What changes is everything else.
//
// Harmony over the pedal. The cell stays in D; the chords above it move every
// two bars, not every bar - slow harmonic rhythm over a fixed bass is the whole
// point of a pedal, and a fast one would cancel it:
//
//   Dm . | F . | Bb . | A .
//
// Against a D in the bass, F is D minor with the root's weight kept, Bb makes it
// a Bb major over its third - the moment of lift - and A is the dominant with
// its C# grinding a half step against the pedal's D. That grind is the piece.
//
// The ward tightens. The `rite` section moves the entire band up one semitone,
// to E flat minor, and the pedal moves with it: the cell is the same pattern,
// written once, used as `cell+1`. A semitone is the smallest move there is and
// the most unsettling - nothing about the music changes except that it is now in
// the wrong place - and then `out` drops back to D, which is the only resolution
// the piece offers.
//
// What each instrument is for, because they are not six copies of the riff:
//
//   Bass       the cell. Sixteenths, but played: the accented notes are the
//              skeleton and the ones marked `+` are dead ghosts - the string
//              damped, the pick still moving. Ghosts are what makes a sixteenth
//              line a bass player instead of a sequencer, and they are the thing
//              the first version of this score had none of. The last note of
//              each bar slides into the next.
//
//   Guitar     not a second riff. It is the engine: palm-muted chugs on the
//              pedal, sixteenths, low and dead, with a power chord stab where
//              the harmony turns over. Chords are root-fifth-octave and never
//              contain a third, since distortion turns a third into a note
//              outside the chord, and the organ has the thirds anyway.
//
//   Organ      the voice. This ensemble is a Hammond and the tune belongs to it -
//              a melody that arrives late, in the verse, over music the ear has
//              already learned, and comes back an octave up when the ward moves.
//
//   Pad        the chord quality the guitar refuses to state: the third and the
//              seventh, two notes, held, swelling into each harmonic change.
//
//   Keys       only in the rite, and only the cell's own shape two octaves up,
//              so the tightening is heard as the same music in a brighter place.
//
//   Drums      the source kits are a two-sound drum machine: kick and an electric
//              snare, almost nothing else. Written as three limbs, but the right
//              hand stays off the cymbals until the rite - it has nothing to play
//              that the sixteenths are not already playing, and an empty hand is
//              what makes the rite's entry land.
//
// Form is entrances: bass alone, then the engine, then the drums lean in, then
// the tune, then the ward moves. Nothing is ever taken away until `out`.

title: Sealed Ward
ensemble: tonewheel
parts: lead guitar keys bass pad perc
tempo: 132
meter: 4/4
key: d minor
order: intro [riff verse rite break reprise] out

// --- the cell, written once ---------------------------------------------

pattern cell
  | d2:0.25! d2:0.25+ d2:0.25 d2:0.25+ f2:0.25! d2:0.25+ c2:0.25 d2:0.25+ a1:0.25! a1:0.25+ c2:0.25 d2:0.25+ f2:0.25! g2:0.25+ f2:0.25 d2:0.25/ |
  | d2:0.25! d2:0.25+ d2:0.25 f2:0.25+ g2:0.25! f2:0.25+ d2:0.25 c2:0.25+ d2:0.25! e2:0.25+ f2:0.25 g2:0.25+ a2:0.25! g2:0.25+ f2:0.25 e2:0.25/ |

// The engine. Twelve dead sixteenths and a stab, then the same bar with the
// stab pushed onto the offbeats - the only syncopation the guitar has, so it
// counts when it happens.

pattern chug
  | d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ [d3 a3 d4]:1! |
  | d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ [d3 a3 d4]:0.5! d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ [d3 a3 d4]:0.5! d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ r:0.5 |

// The cell's shape, two octaves up, for the rite only.

pattern bright
  | d4:0.25! d4:0.25 a4:0.25 d5:0.25 f5:0.25! d5:0.25 c5:0.25 a4:0.25 a4:0.25! c5:0.25 d5:0.25 f5:0.25 a5:0.25! g5:0.25 f5:0.25 d5:0.25 |
  | d5:0.25! a4:0.25 f4:0.25 d4:0.25 g4:0.25! d5:0.25 f5:0.25 g5:0.25 a5:0.25! g5:0.25 f5:0.25 e5:0.25 d5:0.25! f5:0.25 a5:0.25 d6:0.25 |

// --- the kit ------------------------------------------------------------
// The kick answers the cell's accents; the snare takes 2 and 4 and ghosts the
// sixteenth the bass leaves open.

pattern hook
  // The tune, named because the reprise plays it note for note and a reprise
  // that is retyped is a reprise that drifts. `from:verse` cannot carry it
  // there, because declaring a lane in the inheriting section replaces the
  // inherited one outright - and the reprise needs to replace it, to spin the
  // Leslie up under the same notes.
  | d4:0.75! f4:0.75 g4:0.5 a4:0.25 c5:0.25 a4:0.5 g4:0.5 f4:0.5 |
  | d5:1.5_ c5:0.5 bb4:1 a4:1 |
  | a4:0.75! c5:0.75 d5:0.5 f5:0.25 a5:0.25 f5:0.5 e5:0.5 c5:0.5 |
  | f5:1.5_ e5:0.5 d5:1 c5:1 |
  | d4:0.75! f4:0.75 g4:0.5 bb4:0.25 d5:0.25 bb4:0.5 a4:0.5 f4:0.5 |
  | bb4:1.5_ a4:0.5 g4:1 f4:1 |
  | a4:0.5 c#5:0.5 e5:1! g5:0.5 e5:0.5 c#5:1 |
  | c#5:2! e5:0.5 g5:0.5 a5:0.5 g5:0.5 |

pattern feet
  | kick:1! kick:0.5 kick:0.5 kick:1! kick:0.75 kick:0.25 |
pattern back
  | r:1 snare_dry:0.75! snare_dry:0.25. r:1 snare_dry:1! |
pattern hats
  | hat:0.5! hat:0.5. hat:0.5 hat:0.5. hat:0.5 hat:0.5. hat:0.5 hat:0.5. |
pattern four
  | kick:1! kick:1 kick:1! kick:1 |
pattern offbeat
  | r:0.5 hat_open:0.5 r:0.5 hat_open:0.5 r:0.5 hat_open:0.5 r:0.5 hat_open:0.5 |

// --- sections -----------------------------------------------------------

section intro bars:4
  // The cell twice, alone but for the foot. Nothing to hear but the ghosts.
  bass dyn:mp..mf feel:tight art:marcato pocket:on
    | cell | cell |
  perc.feet dyn:mp feel:tight
    | r:4 | r:4 | feet | feet |
  pad dyn:pp
    | [f4 a4]:4 | [f4 a4]:4 | [f4 a4]:4 | [f4 a4]:4^ |

section riff bars:8
  // The engine starts. Still no tune, no cymbals, no chord change for two bars
  // at a time - the ear is being given the pedal to hold on to.
  bass dyn:mf feel:tight art:marcato pocket:on
    | cell | cell | cell | cell |
  guitar dyn:mf..f feel:tight art:sustain pocket:on
    | chug | chug | chug | chug |
  perc.feet dyn:mf feel:tight
    | feet | feet | feet | feet | feet | feet | feet |
    | kick:1! kick:0.5 kick:0.5 kick:0.5 kick:0.5 kick:0.5 kick:0.5 |
  perc.left dyn:mf feel:tight
    | back | back | back | back | back | back | back |
    | r:1 snare_dry:0.75! snare_dry:0.25. snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25! snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25! snare_dry:0.25! snare_dry:0.25! |
  pad dyn:pp..p
    | [f4 a4]:4 | [f4 a4]:4 | [a4 c5]:4 | [a4 c5]:4^ |
    | [d4 f4]:4 | [d4 f4]:4 | [c#4 g4]:4 | [c#4 g4]:4^ |

section verse bars:8
  // The organ arrives. Bar 3 is bar 1 moved up to sit on the F, and bar 5 the
  // same shape again over the Bb - the tune is one idea heard three times at
  // three heights, which is how a melody gets remembered. The long notes are
  // the thirds and sevenths the guitar will not play.
  lead dyn:mf..f feel:tight pocket:lay rot:slow
    // The rotor is turning slowly when the tune arrives - chorale, the speed a
    // Hammond idles at. It has somewhere to go later.
    | hook |
  bass dyn:mf feel:tight art:marcato pocket:lay
    | cell | cell | cell | cell |
  guitar dyn:mf feel:tight art:sustain pocket:lay
    | chug | chug | chug | chug |
  perc.feet dyn:mf feel:tight
    | feet | feet | feet | feet | feet | feet | feet |
    | kick:1! kick:0.5 kick:0.5 kick:1! kick:0.5 kick:0.5 |
  perc.left dyn:mf feel:tight
    | back | back | back |
    | r:1 snare_dry:0.75! snare_dry:0.25. r:1 snare_dry:0.5! tom_floor:0.5 |
    | back | back | back |
    | r:1 snare_dry:0.75! snare_dry:0.25. tom_high:0.5 tom_high:0.5 tom_mid:0.5 tom_floor:0.5 |
  pad dyn:p
    | [f4 a4]:4 | [f4 a4]:4 | [a4 c5]:4 | [a4 c5]:4^ |
    | [d4 f4]:4 | [d4 f4]:4 | [c#4 g4]:4 | [c#4 g4]:4^ |

section rite bars:8
  // The lift. The bass never moves - the pedal is the thing the whole piece
  // stands on, and taking it away was what made the first attempt at this
  // section fall over. Instead the guitar's roots climb away from it, Bb C Dm
  // A, two bars each: bVI to bVII to i is the oldest lift in this idiom, and
  // against a bass that refuses to follow, each chord is heard as a tension
  // rather than a change of scene.
  //
  // It is also not louder than the verse until it has earned it. The keys stay
  // out for four bars, the right hand plays offbeats rather than filling every
  // eighth, and the dynamic climbs across the section instead of starting at
  // the top.
  lead dyn:mf..ff feel:tight pocket:push rot:fast
    | bb4:0.5! d5:0.5 f5:1! d5:0.5 c5:0.5 bb4:1 |
    | d5:1.5_ f5:0.5 a5:1 f5:1 |
    | c5:0.5! e5:0.5 g5:1! e5:0.5 d5:0.5 c5:1 |
    | e5:1.5_ g5:0.5 c6:1 a5:1 |
    | d5:0.5! f5:0.5 a5:1! g5:0.5 f5:0.5 d5:1 |
    | a5:1.5_ g5:0.5 f5:1 d5:1 |
    | c#5:0.5! e5:0.5 a5:1! g5:0.5 e5:0.5 c#5:1 |
    | c#5:1! e5:1 g5:0.5 a5:0.5 bb5:0.5! a5:0.5 |
  keys dyn:mf..f feel:tight pocket:push
    // Held back until the second phrase, so the section still has somewhere
    // to go when it is halfway through.
    | r:4 | r:4 | r:4 | r:4 |
    | bright | bright |
  bass dyn:f feel:tight art:marcato pocket:push
    | cell | cell | cell | cell |
  guitar dyn:mf..ff feel:tight art:sustain pocket:push
    | chug-4 | chug-2 | chug | chug-5 |
  perc.right dyn:mf..ff feel:tight
    | crash_big:0.5! r:0.5 hat_open:0.5 r:0.5 hat_open:0.5 r:0.5 hat_open:0.5 r:0.5 |
    | offbeat | offbeat |
    | r:0.5 hat_open:0.5 r:0.5 hat_open:0.5 r:2 |
    | crash:0.5! r:0.5 hat_open:0.5 r:0.5 hat_open:0.5 r:0.5 hat_open:0.5 r:0.5 |
    | offbeat | offbeat |
    | crash_big:0.5! r:1.5 crash:0.5! r:1.5 |
  perc.feet dyn:mf..ff feel:tight
    | feet | feet | feet | feet |
    | four | four | four |
    | kick:0.5! kick:0.5 kick:0.5 kick:0.5 kick:0.5! kick:0.5 kick:0.5! kick:0.5! |
  perc.left dyn:mf..ff feel:tight
    | back | back | back |
    | r:1 snare_dry:0.75! snare_dry:0.25. r:0.5 snare_dry:0.5! snare_dry:0.5 snare_dry:0.5! |
    | back | back | back |
    | snare_dry:0.25. snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25! snare_dry:0.25. snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25! snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25! snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25! snare_dry:0.25! snare_dry:0.25! snare_dry:0.25! |
  pad dyn:p..mf
    | [d4 f4]:4 | [d4 f4]:4 | [e4 g4]:4 | [e4 g4]:4^ |
    | [f4 a4]:4 | [f4 a4]:4 | [c#4 g4]:4 | [c#4 g4]:4^ |

section break bars:8
  // The drop, and the only release the piece has. Guitar and kit stop dead and
  // the cell is naked again, exactly as it was in the intro - a piece that
  // returns to its own opening three quarters of the way through is heard as
  // whole rather than as a list of sections. Over it the organ stops playing a
  // tune and plays notes: two, three beats each, the long chord tones the
  // sixteenths never leave room for.
  //
  // The kit comes back alone in the last two bars and drags the band in with it.
  bass dyn:mp feel:loose art:marcato pocket:lay
    | cell | cell | cell | cell |
  lead dyn:p..mf feel:loose pocket:lay rot:slow
    | d5:2_ c5:2_ |
    | bb4:3_ a4:1 |
    | f5:2_ e5:2_ |
    | d5:4_ |
    | a4:2_ c5:2_ |
    | d5:3_ f5:1 |
    | e5:2! c#5:2_ |
    | d5:1.5! a4:0.5 f4:1 a4:1 |
  perc.left dyn:p..f feel:tight
    | r:4 | r:4 | r:4 | r:4 | r:4 | r:4 |
    | r:2 snare_dry:0.5. snare_dry:0.5 snare_dry:0.5. snare_dry:0.5 |
    | snare_dry:0.25. snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25. snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25! snare_dry:0.25. snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25! snare_dry:0.25! snare_dry:0.25! snare_dry:0.25! snare_dry:0.25! |
  perc.feet dyn:p..f feel:tight
    | r:4 | r:4 | r:4 | r:4 | r:4 | r:4 |
    | kick:2! r:2 |
    | kick:1! kick:1 kick:1! kick:0.5 kick:0.5 |
  pad dyn:p
    | [f4 a4]:4 | [f4 a4]:4 | [d4 f4]:4 | [d4 f4]:4^ |
    | [a4 c5]:4 | [a4 c5]:4 | [c#4 g4]:4 | [c#4 g4]:4^ |

section reprise from:verse
  // The hook returns note for note - `from:verse` copies the organ, the bass,
  // the pad and the kit's two hands unchanged, because the whole point of a
  // reprise is that it is the same thing. What is new is underneath and above
  // it: the guitar leans on the dynamic, the keys double the cell two octaves
  // up for the first time outside the rite, and the right hand finally plays
  // straight eighths, which is the sound of a band all the way in.
  lead dyn:f..ff feel:tight pocket:lay rot:fast
    // The same eight bars as the verse, from the same pattern, but the Leslie
    // is up this time. That is the whole difference and it is enough: a
    // reprise is not the tune played harder, it is the tune in a room that
    // has changed.
    | hook |
  guitar dyn:f..ff feel:tight art:sustain pocket:on
    | chug | chug | chug | chug |
  keys dyn:mf..f feel:tight pocket:on
    | bright | bright | bright | bright |
  perc.right dyn:f..ff feel:tight
    | crash_big:0.5! hat:0.5. hat:0.5 hat:0.5. hat:0.5 hat:0.5. hat:0.5 hat:0.5. |
    | hats | hats | hats |
    | crash:0.5! hat:0.5. hat:0.5 hat:0.5. hat:0.5 hat:0.5. hat:0.5 hat:0.5. |
    | hats | hats |
    | crash_big:0.5! r:1.5 crash:0.5! r:1.5 |

section out bars:4
  // Back to D, which after the rite is the only thing that sounds like relief.
  // The cell runs one last time and stops on its own first note.
  bass dyn:f..mf feel:tight art:marcato pocket:on
    | cell |
    | d2:0.25! d2:0.25+ d2:0.25 d2:0.25+ f2:0.25! d2:0.25+ c2:0.25 d2:0.25+ a1:0.25! a1:0.25+ c2:0.25 d2:0.25+ a1:0.5! a1:0.5/ |
    | d2:4! |
  guitar dyn:f..mf feel:tight art:sustain pocket:on
    | chug |
    | d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ d3:0.25+ [c#3 g#3 c#4]:1! |
    | [d3 a3 d4]:4! |
  lead dyn:f..mf feel:tight
    | d5:1! a4:1 f4:1 d4:1 |
    | c#5:1.5! e5:0.5 g5:1 a5:1 |
    | a4:2_ f4:1 e4:1 |
    | d4:4_ |
  perc.right dyn:f..mf feel:tight
    | crash:0.5! r:3.5 | r:4 | r:2 crash_small:0.5! r:1.5 | crash_big:4! |
  perc.feet dyn:f..mf feel:tight
    | feet | feet |
    | kick:1! kick:0.5 kick:0.5 kick:0.5 kick:0.5 kick:0.5 kick:0.5 |
    | kick:4! |
  perc.left dyn:f..mf feel:tight
    | back | back |
    | r:1 snare_dry:0.75! snare_dry:0.25. snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25! snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25 snare_dry:0.25! snare_dry:0.25! snare_dry:0.25! |
    | r:4 |
  pad dyn:mf..p
    | [f4 a4]:4 | [c#4 g4]:4 | [c#4 g4]:4^ | [d4 f4 a4]:4 |
